        "original_id": "ee209bc9-d36a-5744-86df-31ba2b6ec31e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Félix du Temple de la Croix\n- Topics: early flying machines, powered flight\n- Products: powered model plane, Monoplane\n\nFacts:\n- Félix du Temple de la Croix developed some of the first flying machines.\n- In 1857, Félix du Temple de la Croix is credited with the first successful flight of a powered aircraft of any sort, using a powered model plane.\n- In 1874, Félix du Temple de la Croix is sometimes credited with the first manned powered flight in history aboard his Monoplane.\n- Early flying machines include all forms of aircraft that were studied or constructed before the development of the modern aeroplane by 1910.",
